  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Comprehensive Reintegration Programme in Areas of Returns in Burundi (Phase III)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">In May 2020, Burundi held its first general elections since 2015. During the previous electoral cycle, political instability coupled with natural disasters forced more than 267,000 Burundians to flee the country and resulted in the internal displacement of 202,000 persons. Since the inauguration of the new government in June 2020, the country has witnessed notable improvements in terms of its security, political, and socioeconomic situation. Building on progress already achieved in the two previous projects phases, this project aims to provide reintegration assistance to approximately 54,770 people (returnees, host community members, and other types of displaced and affected peoples alike). These interventions coincide with the anticipated return of 70,000 new individuals from the United Republic of Tanzania and the Republic of Rwanda during 2022. The general objective of this project is to contribute to national efforts in strengthening the reintegration capacity for Burundian returnees and displaced populations within communities.</narrative>
  </description>
